ClipAgent -- Win7 x64 / Win11 x64 clipboard agent (pull model)
===============================================================

Layout
  parts\\*.part        source fragments, one per delivery turn
  merge.bat           concatenate parts -> real files, then build
  ClipProtocol.h      wire format, shared by both ends
  miniz.h / miniz.c   built-in store-only ZIP writer (NOT upstream miniz)
  ClipAgent.cpp       main program, delivered in 4 segments
  build.bat           cl /MT /utf-8 /SUBSYSTEM:CONSOLE,6.01
  run-host.bat        Win11 side, auto reconnect
  run-guest.bat       Win7 side, auto reconnect
  install-autorun.bat HKCU Run key, no admin needed
  release\\ClipAgent.exe

Build
  1. Open a VS x64 Native Tools Command Prompt.
  2. merge.bat --no-build     (check every [have])
  3. merge.bat                (assemble + build -> release\\ClipAgent.exe)

Run
  Host (Win11):
    ClipAgent.exe --listen 8080 --key mon --outdir D:\\ClipInbox
  Guest (Win7):
    ClipAgent.exe --connect 192.168.1.50:8080 --key mon --outdir C:\\ClipInbox
  Options:
    --key <s>           shared LAN label, NOT encryption
    --outdir <dir>      fallback landing directory
    --max-file-mb <n>   ask before sending above n MB (default 256)
    --confirm-mb <n>    warn level (default 50)
    --quiet             hide console, tray only
    --help              show usage

Hotkeys (only way to trigger a transfer)
  Ctrl+Alt+V   paste remote content (PULL). In PAUSED state: resume.
  Ctrl+Alt+C   cancel current transfer.
  Ctrl+Alt+S   show / hide the log window.

Model
  Copying advertises only. FRAME_LIST carries a fixed-size summary and
  ZERO file bytes. Nothing is transmitted until the far end presses
  Ctrl+Alt+V, which sends FRAME_PULL. Files and folders are packed into
  a temp ZIP (store method) and streamed in 64 KiB chunks. Clipboard
  text is streamed the same way and goes to CF_UNICODETEXT, no file.

Encoding
  Every delivered source file is pure ASCII (every byte < 0x80).
  Chinese UI text appears only as L"\\uXXXX" wide literals in
  ClipAgent.cpp part 03. No BOM is required anywhere. .bat files MUST
  stay BOM-free or cmd.exe misparses the first line. build.bat passes
  /utf-8 as a harmless safety net.
  Check: powershell -NoProfile -Command "$b=[IO.File]::ReadAllBytes('ClipAgent.cpp'); ($b|?{$_ -gt 0x7F}).Count"

Invariants
  1. Copying never transfers data. Only Ctrl+Alt+V pulls.
  2. Peak heap stays at one 64 KiB buffer per side, independent of
     file size. The receiver writes chunks straight to disk.
  3. The temp zip is deleted on EVERY exit path, success or failure.
  4. At most one ClipAgent_*.zip in %TEMP% and one *.part in outdir.
  5. Cleanup is idempotent and every exit routes through it.
  6. T1 user cancel / T2 peer cancel / T3 disconnect / T4 crash are
     all covered: T1/T2/T3 by CleanupTransfer, T4 by the startup and
     exit sweep plus a 60s no-reply -> auto pause.
  7. Pause keeps the .part breakpoint for 30 minutes, then sweeps.
  8. An occupied target names the owner process and PID.
  9. Critical system processes are never terminated by the agent.
 10. Skipped entries are recorded in the ZIP archive comment and the
     receiver always shows them.
 11. Frames are validated: magic, version, keyTag, length cap, CRC32.
 12. Landing names never contain \\ / : * ? " < > | or control chars.
 13. Both ends sanitize independently; the receiver trusts nothing.
 14. Reserved device names, trailing dot/space and NTFS ADS colons
     are all handled.
 15. ZIP entry segments containing ".." or a drive root are skipped
     and reported.
 16. All delivered sources are pure ASCII; Chinese only as \\uXXXX.

Acceptance tests
  A. Kill the agent with Task Manager, restart: zero leftover
     ClipAgent_*.zip / *.part anywhere.
  B. Cancel 10 times in a row: zero leftovers.
  C. Unplug the vNIC for 1s, plug back: state returns to IDLE,
     zero leftovers, user just presses Ctrl+Alt+V again.
  D. Copy a folder, paste: lands as a single .zip, extracted by user.
  E. Copy a 10GB file: peak memory stays flat, no OOM.
  E2. Open the target file in Notepad, paste: the dialog names
     notepad.exe (PID xxxx) and offers terminate/pause/skip/cancel.
  E3. Target under a driver-protected path: ACCESS_DENIED path prints
     the "check your minifilter/ObCallback" hint and never kills the
     driver by itself.
  F. Pause, then Ctrl+Alt+V: resumes from the breakpoint; rename is
     retried when the .part is already complete.
  G. Name traps: "..\\evil:stream.txt", "sub/a.txt", "CON.txt",
     "a.txt." all land as safe single filenames inside outdir only.
  H. build.bat under a non-Chinese system locale still compiles with
     no C4819.

Troubleshooting
  WSAStartup / bind failed      : port in use, change --listen port.
  hotkey unavailable            : another app owns Ctrl+Alt+V; the
                                  tray menu still works.
  advert send failed            : peer not connected, check run-guest.
  crc/size mismatch             : transfer dropped, press Ctrl+Alt+V.
  access denied on landing      : check protected dir, read-only
                                  attribute, or your own minifilter.
  timestamp service unreachable : signtool failed only; the unsigned
                                  binary is kept and still runs.